1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From http://osten-sacken.h1.ru/text3_10.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1855 "A Book of Russia's Noble Families" by Duke Piotr Dolgorukij was published in Saint Petersburg. This is what it tells us: the family of von der Osten genannt Sakken is one of the oldest and most significant noble families 
2 CONC in the Baltic lands. It originated from Austria and later on moved via Pomerania to the Baltic. Balduin von Sakken, a baron of the Teutonic Order, participated in the 1205-year crusade. Both Otto and Wedeghe von Sakken were knight
2 CONC s of the Livonian Order (mentioned in 1457), whereas Dionisius von Sakken was an envoy of the Order of the Knights of the Sword to the Holy See in Rome (1500). 
