1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Starost von Dt. Krone und Dalcz  // Wałcz III - 719 // Wałcz I - 2444, 2443, 2498,  // Wałcz - 2502, 2524, 2767, 2780, 2791 [? jako Prawdzic], 2799 [? jako Prawdzic], 2803, 2883, 2904, 2932, 2941, 2950, 2960, 2976,
2 CONC  3092, 3094, 3145
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Not to be confused with http://www.geneagraphie.com/getperson.php?personID=I601724&tree=1 Heinrich von der Goltz, son of Heinrich von der Goltz and Elizabeth Dorothea von der Goltz.
2 CONT
2 CONT The information at Wielka Genealogia Minakowskiego | http://wielcy.pl/wgm/?m=NG&t=PN&n=6.435.115, the genealogical database maintained by Marek Jerzy Minakowski, is not correct.  Marek confuses this Henryk with another older Golcz
2 CONC  cousin also named Henryk who was starost of Wałcz.  The two cousins interacted with one another on financial and property deals, as in the Teki Dworzaczka records, but our Henryk was (Christian Heinrich Günter von der Goltz), hei
2 CONC r of Lubno (Lüben), Jabłonowo (Appelwerder) and Starost of Derpt (Polish name of this town still unknown). He later sold both Lubno and Jabłonowo to obtain Brotzen (Broczyno, southeast of Czaplinek).
2 CONT
2 CONT After careful study of both Henryks, it becomes clear that our Henryk married to Zofia Elzbieta Osterling was the "Henryk of Lubno" - NOT the Henryk of Wałcz.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Our Henryk of Lubno was the son of Günther Johann von der Goltz, who was born 27 Dec 1697 in Lüben (Lubno), and who died in 1749 in Brotzen (Broczyno, southeast of Czaplinek), and of Dorothea von Borcke (who was the daughter of Wo
2 CONC lff Jürgen von Borcke and Ilsa Sophie von Podewils).
